                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_210\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit changes a single line in FlexReader.java:\n\n    file.field = field % runCount;\n->  file.field = field % (nFiles / (wellCount * runCount));\n\nTracing the history of this exact assignment across the candidates:\n\n- candidate_149 introduces the FlexFile/field-indexing logic with `file.field = field;` (no run-count math at all).\n- candidate_202 changes this to `file.field = field / runCount;`, alongside adding `file.acquisition` and run-directory tracking to support multiple runs.\n- candidate_210 changes the expression again, from `file.field = field / runCount;` to `file.field = field % runCount;` \u2014 this is the exact buggy expression that appears immediately before the fix.\n- candidate_211 applies the fix itself, replacing `field % runCount` with `field % (nFiles / (wellCount * runCount))`, matching fix_commit_diff.txt exactly.\n\nSince the fix directly reverses/corrects the `field % runCount` computation, and candidate_210 is the commit that introduced that specific expression (switching from division to modulo by runCount), candidate_210 is the bug-introducing commit. The bug: when multiple runs are present, computing the field index as `field % runCount` does not correctly account for the total number of files, wells, and runs, causing incorrect file indexing. The fix corrects the divisor to `nFiles / (wellCount * runCount)` so the modulo operation produces the correct per-well field count.\n"
